Copy dependencies to _[root]/lib_ directory during package phase. Also Build Helper Maven Plugin to generate a property for the project root folder, using it from Maven Dependency Plugin. This can come in
handy in many situations.

@jkesselm, this should help you run the tests from _xalan-test_ against a clean Maven build, too.

## Alterado o tamanho do pacote para dois caracteres
Antes
```c
typedef struct pack_of_paper {
    int cod_pack_of_paper;
    int cod_type_of_paper;
    int amount_of_papers;
    char amount[4];
    int cod_brand;
    float price;
} PackOfPaper;
```

Depois
```c
typedef struct pack_of_paper {
    int cod_pack_of_paper;
    int cod_type_of_paper;
    int amount_of_papers;
    char amount[3];
    int cod_brand;
    float price;
} PackOfPaper;
```

Configured husky.
Plugin husky has folder .husky with configs. Before commit, husky use git hook pre-commited and call "npx lint-staged" from package.json
`"lint-staged": {
    "*.{tsx,js,html}": [
      "eslint"
    ]
  },` 
  Here we can add file extensions to check like .scss 
  
  For rule `"@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any": "error"`, use _typeAny_
  For rule _"no-console": "error"_, use _// eslint-disable-next-line no-console_

Aggregate parsers is a more flexible version of the compound parser.

Example:
```java
final AggregateCommandParser<CommandSender, Location> locationParser = AggregateCommandParser<CommandSender>builder()
    .withComponent("world", worldParser())
    .withComponent("x", integerParser())
    .withComponent("y", integerParser())
    .withComponent("z", integerParser())
    .withMapper(Location.class, (commandContext, aggregateCommandContext) -> {
        final World world = aggregateCommandContext.get("world");
        final int x = aggregateCommandContext.get("x");
        final int y = aggregateCommandContext.get("y");
        final int z = aggregateCommandContext.get("z");
        return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(new Location(world, x, y, z));
     }).build();
```

